 "verdict": "inconsistent: with signs labelled by the letter they look like, the alignment to the record's plaintext gives 40% letter / 45% skeleton consistency over repeated shapes, far from a key. The sign COUNT fits (81 signs by eye, 17+13+13+18+12+8 as in the record, against 80 letters with lam-alif as one letter), and the cipher's only repeated 3- and 4-sign runs fall where the plaintext repeats (GH D Lo at signs 1 and 41 = بني twice; W E8 A W at signs 24 and 71 = the two ذلك قد), so the plaintext is the right text; the failure is in my shape classes (letter-shaped signs lumped together, e.g. Lo) and in the plaintext's doubtful words. Not keyed.",
